-- Tests for the documents-defamation group: Chapters 18, 21 and 22 of the
-- Penal Code 1871 (ss 463-507; Chapter 20 and ss 508-510 are repealed).
--
-- Expected values come FROM THE SOURCE: every Illustration that can be
-- expressed on the atoms is an #ASSERT, cited on the line above it. The
-- charge texts are this encoding's recital template (CPC ss 123-125) and are
-- asserted as text so that a change to the template is visible.
--
-- FIXTURES. L4 has no record-update operator, so each family has a
-- constructor that takes the LIST of leaves that hold, by a short key; every
-- other leaf is FALSE - which is also what the charge generator's schema
-- completion does with an unknown leaf. A key the constructor does not know
-- is simply never TRUE, so a misspelt key makes a test fail loudly rather
-- than pass quietly: every positive Illustration below would fail.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-common`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-forgery`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-currency`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-defamation`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-intimidation`

§ `Tests - documents-defamation`

§§ `Shared particulars`

GIVEN accused IS A STRING
GIVETH A Particulars
`test particulars for` accused MEANS
    Particulars WITH
        accused            IS accused
        date               IS "1 March 2026"
        time               IS ""
        place              IS "Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1"
        `co-accused`       IS ""
        `common intention` IS FALSE

§ `Chapter 18 - forgery`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN document IS A STRING
      manner   IS A STRING
      keys     IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Forgery Facts`
`forgery facts` document manner keys MEANS
    `Forgery Facts` WITH
        particulars           IS `test particulars for` "A"
        `the document`        IS document
        `the manner`          IS manner
        `a document`          IS elem "document" keys
        `an electronic record` IS elem "electronic record" keys
        dishonestly           IS elem "dishonestly" keys
        fraudulently          IS elem "fraudulently" keys
        `makes, signs, seals or executes a document or part of a document` IS elem "(a)(i)" keys
        `makes any electronic record or part of any electronic record` IS elem "(a)(ii)" keys
        `affixes any electronic signature on any electronic record` IS elem "(a)(iii)" keys
        `makes any mark denoting the execution of a document or the authenticity of the electronic signature` IS elem "(a)(iv)" keys
        `intending it to be believed that it was made by or by the authority of a person by whom or by whose authority he knows it was not made` IS elem "(a) as by another" keys
        `intending it to be believed that it was made at a time at which he knows it was not made` IS elem "(a) as at another time" keys
        `without lawful authority` IS elem "(b) without lawful authority" keys
        `alters a document or an electronic record in any material part after it has been made or executed` IS elem "(b) alters" keys
        `causes any person to sign, seal, execute or alter a document or an electronic record, or to affix his electronic signature` IS elem "(c) causes to sign" keys
        `knowing that such person by reason of unsoundness of mind or intoxication cannot know the contents or the nature of the alteration` IS elem "(c) unsoundness" keys
        `knowing that such person by reason of deception practised upon him does not know the contents or the nature of the alteration` IS elem "(c) deception" keys
        `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` IS elem "intent: damage" keys
        `with intent to support any claim or title` IS elem "intent: claim" keys
        `with intent to cause any person to part with property` IS elem "intent: property" keys
        `with intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract` IS elem "intent: contract" keys
        `with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed` IS elem "intent: fraud" keys
        `purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice` IS elem "466: court record" keys
        `purports to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial` IS elem "466: register of births" keys
        `purports to be a register kept by a public servant as such` IS elem "466: public register" keys
        `purports to be a certificate or document made by a public servant in his official capacity` IS elem "466: official certificate" keys
        `purports to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, or to take any proceedings therein, or to confess judgment` IS elem "466: authority for a suit" keys
        `purports to be a power of attorney` IS elem "466: power of attorney" keys
        `purports to be a valuable security` IS elem "467: valuable security" keys
        `purports to be a will` IS elem "467: will" keys
        `purports to be an authority to adopt a child` IS elem "467: adoption" keys
        `purports to give authority to make or transfer any valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends thereon` IS elem "467: authority over a security" keys
        `purports to give authority to receive or deliver any money, movable property or valuable security` IS elem "467: authority to receive money" keys
        `purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money` IS elem "467: receipt for money" keys
        `purports to be an acquittance or receipt for the delivery of any movable property or valuable security` IS elem "467: receipt for property" keys
        `intending that the document forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating` IS elem "468: for cheating" keys
        `intending that the document forged shall harm the reputation of any person` IS elem "469: intending harm to reputation" keys
        `knowing that it is likely to be used to harm the reputation of any person` IS elem "469: knowing likely harm to reputation" keys

-- An Illustration's facts, where only the keys matter.
GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Forgery Facts`
`an illustrated forgery` keys MEANS `forgery facts` "the document in the Illustration" "" keys

§§ `s 464 Illustrations (each: "A has committed forgery")`

-- s 464 illus (a): A adds a cypher to Z's letter of credit for $1,000, making it
-- $10,000, to defraud B, intending B to believe Z so wrote it. Making PART of
-- a document, as by Z (FORK DD-1 on which limb).
`illus 464(a)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: fraud", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `makes a false document or false electronic record` `illus 464(a)`
#ASSERT `commits forgery` `illus 464(a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 467` `illus 464(a)`

-- s 464 illus (b): A, without Z's authority, affixes Z's seal to a conveyance
-- from Z to A, to sell the estate to B and obtain the purchase money.
`illus 464(b)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(b)`

-- s 464 illus (c): A fraudulently fills up a blank cheque signed by B with $1,000.
`illus 464(c)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(c)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 467` `illus 464(c)`

-- s 464 illus (d): B, authorised to fill in up to $1,000, fraudulently fills in
-- $10,000 - making part of the cheque as by A's authority, knowing A did not
-- authorise it.
`illus 464(d)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(d)`

-- s 464 illus (e): A draws a bill on himself in B's name without authority,
-- to discount it with a banker as though secured by B.
`illus 464(e)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(e)`

-- s 464 illus (f): A dishonestly scratches B's name out of Z's will, so that
-- the whole seems left to A and C - alteration in a material part.
`illus 464(f)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "(b) without lawful authority", "(b) alters", "intent: claim", "467: will")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(f)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 467` `illus 464(f)`

-- s 464 illus (g): B dishonestly erases "Pay to Z or his order", turning a
-- special endorsement into a blank one.
`illus 464(g)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "(b) without lawful authority", "(b) alters", "intent: property", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(g)`

-- s 464 illus (h): A, having conveyed an estate to Z, executes a conveyance to B
-- dated 6 months earlier, to defraud Z.
`illus 464(h)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as at another time", "intent: fraud")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(h)`

-- s 464 illus (i): A writes a different legatee into the will Z dictated, and
-- by telling Z it is as instructed, induces Z to sign it.
`illus 464(i)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(c) causes to sign", "(c) deception", "intent: claim", "467: will")
#ASSERT `makes a false document or false electronic record` `illus 464(i)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 467` `illus 464(i)`

-- s 464 illus (j): A writes a begging letter signed in B's name to obtain alms
-- from Z - "a false document in order to induce Z to part with property".
`illus 464(j)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(j)`

-- s 464 illus (k): A writes a character certificate in B's name to obtain
-- employment under Z - intent to induce Z to enter into a contract for service.
`illus 464(k)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: contract")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464(k)`

§§ `Explanation 1 Illustrations - a man's signature of his own name`

-- Expl 1 illus (a): A signs his own name to a bill, meaning it to be believed
-- drawn by another person of the same name.
`illus 464 Expl 1(a)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: fraud", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464 Expl 1(a)`

-- Expl 1 illus (b): A writes "accepted" and signs Z's name, so that B may write
-- a bill on the paper and negotiate it as accepted by Z. (B's liability, if he
-- knowingly draws the bill, is the same ladder on B's facts.)
`illus 464 Expl 1(b)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: fraud")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464 Expl 1(b)`

-- Expl 1 illus (c): A endorses in his own name a bill payable to another of the
-- same name, meaning it to be believed that person endorsed it.
`illus 464 Expl 1(c)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464 Expl 1(c)`

-- Expl 1 illus (d): B antedates, in his own name, a lease to Z, to defraud A
-- and make it seem granted before the seizure.
`illus 464 Expl 1(d)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as at another time", "intent: fraud")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464 Expl 1(d)`

-- Expl 1 illus (e): A antedates a promissory note to defraud his creditors -
-- "forgery under the first head of the definition", i.e. limb (a).
`illus 464 Expl 1(e)` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as at another time", "intent: fraud", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464 Expl 1(e)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 467` `illus 464 Expl 1(e)`

-- Expl 2 illus: A draws a bill on a fictitious person and accepts it in that
-- name, to negotiate it.
`illus 464 Expl 2` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: fraud", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `illus 464 Expl 2`

§§ `Forgery - the boundaries of each element`

-- No s 463 intent: a false document, but not forgery.
`false but no intent` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another")
#ASSERT `makes a false document or false electronic record` `false but no intent`
#ASSERT NOT `commits forgery` `false but no intent`

-- Neither dishonest nor fraudulent: not a false document at all (s 464).
`neither dishonest nor fraudulent` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: fraud")
#ASSERT NOT `makes a false document or false electronic record` `neither dishonest nor fraudulent`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 465` `neither dishonest nor fraudulent`

-- Limb (a): the act without the intention of belief is not enough.
`signed but no false belief intended` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "intent: fraud")
#ASSERT NOT `makes a false document or false electronic record` `signed but no false belief intended`

-- Limb (b): an alteration WITH lawful authority is not a false making.
`altered with authority` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "(b) alters", "intent: claim")
#ASSERT NOT `makes a false document or false electronic record` `altered with authority`

-- Limb (c): causing a signature without knowing of incapacity or deception.
`signature procured, no knowledge` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(c) causes to sign", "intent: claim")
#ASSERT NOT `makes a false document or false electronic record` `signature procured, no knowledge`
`signature procured from a drunk` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(c) causes to sign", "(c) unsoundness", "intent: claim")
#ASSERT `commits forgery` `signature procured from a drunk`

-- An electronic record: forgery (s 463) and s 466, but not s 467, which says
-- "forges a document" (FORK DD-4).
`a forged e-certificate` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "electronic record", "fraudulently", "(a)(ii)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "466: official certificate", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 465` `a forged e-certificate`
#ASSERT `offence under s 466` `a forged e-certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 467` `a forged e-certificate`

-- s 466 needs one of its descriptions; s 467 one of its own.
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 466` `illus 464(b)`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 467` `illus 464(b)`
`a forged power of attorney` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "466: power of attorney")
#ASSERT `offence under s 466` `a forged power of attorney`

-- s 468 and s 469 add an intention to forgery; neither is made out without it.
`forged for cheating` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "468: for cheating")
#ASSERT `offence under s 468` `forged for cheating`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 468` `illus 464(j)`
`forged to smear` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: damage", "469: knowing likely harm to reputation")
#ASSERT `offence under s 469` `forged to smear`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 469` `forged for cheating`
-- ... and s 468's intention without forgery is nothing.
`cheating intent but nothing false` MEANS `an illustrated forgery` (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "intent: property", "468: for cheating")
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 468` `cheating intent but nothing false`

-- s 470
#ASSERT `a forged document or forged electronic record within section 470` `illus 464(j)`
#ASSERT NOT `a forged document or forged electronic record within section 470` `false but no intent`

§§ `Forgery - punishments, as data`

#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 465`'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS JUST 48
#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 465`'s `or with both`
#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 467`'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 467`'s fine EQUALS `shall also be liable to`
#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 468`'s imprisonment EQUALS `shall be punished with`
#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 469`'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS JUST 60

§§ `Forgery - charges as text, and a refusal`

`the medical certificate` MEANS `forgery facts` "a medical certificate dated 1 March 2026 purporting to be issued by Dr Tan Ah Kow" "by signing the name of Dr Tan Ah Kow on it without his authority" (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "(a)(i)", "(a) as by another", "intent: property", "468: for cheating")

#ASSERT (`charge under s 465` `the medical certificate`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 465` `the medical certificate`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did commit forgery by making a false document, to wit, a medical certificate dated 1 March 2026 purporting to be issued by Dr Tan Ah Kow, by signing the name of Dr Tan Ah Kow on it without his authority, with intent to cause any person to part with property, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 465 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 465` `the medical certificate`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, or with fine, or with both"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 468` `the medical certificate`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did commit forgery by making a false document, to wit, a medical certificate dated 1 March 2026 purporting to be issued by Dr Tan Ah Kow, by signing the name of Dr Tan Ah Kow on it without his authority, with intent to cause any person to part with property, intending that the said document shall be used for the purpose of cheating, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 468 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 468` `the medical certificate`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"

-- Refusals name the missing elements, in the section's order.
#ASSERT NOT ((`charge under s 465` `false but no intent`)'s `made out`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 465` `false but no intent`)'s text EQUALS ""
#ASSERT (`charge under s 465` `false but no intent`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 465 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of forgery (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person, or to support any claim or title, or to cause any person to part with property, or to enter into any express or implied contract, or with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed; the elements of section 463 taken together."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 467` `a forged e-certificate`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 467 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of forgery of a valuable security or will (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: a document (section 467 does not extend to an electronic record)."

§§ `ss 471, 474 - using or holding a forged document`

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Forged Document Facts`
`forged document facts` keys MEANS
    `Forged Document Facts` WITH
        particulars           IS `test particulars for` "B"
        `the document`        IS "a Certificate of Entitlement purporting to be issued by the Land Transport Authority"
        `the use`             IS "submitting it to Lim Motor Pte Ltd"
        `a document`          IS elem "document" keys
        `an electronic record` IS elem "electronic record" keys
        `knows it to be a forged document or forged electronic record` IS elem "knows forged" keys
        `has reason to believe it to be a forged document or forged electronic record` IS elem "reason to believe forged" keys
        `uses as genuine`     IS elem "uses as genuine" keys
        dishonestly           IS elem "dishonestly" keys
        fraudulently          IS elem "fraudulently" keys
        `has in his possession` IS elem "possession" keys
        `intending that the same shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine` IS elem "intending use as genuine" keys
        `purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice` IS elem "466: court record" keys
        `purports to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial` IS elem "466: register of births" keys
        `purports to be a register kept by a public servant as such` IS elem "466: public register" keys
        `purports to be a certificate or document made by a public servant in his official capacity` IS elem "466: official certificate" keys
        `purports to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, or to take any proceedings therein, or to confess judgment` IS elem "466: authority for a suit" keys
        `purports to be a power of attorney` IS elem "466: power of attorney" keys
        `purports to be a valuable security` IS elem "467: valuable security" keys
        `purports to be a will` IS elem "467: will" keys
        `purports to be an authority to adopt a child` IS elem "467: adoption" keys
        `purports to give authority to make or transfer any valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends thereon` IS elem "467: authority over a security" keys
        `purports to give authority to receive or deliver any money, movable property or valuable security` IS elem "467: authority to receive money" keys
        `purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money` IS elem "467: receipt for money" keys
        `purports to be an acquittance or receipt for the delivery of any movable property or valuable security` IS elem "467: receipt for property" keys

`the forged COE` MEANS `forged document facts` (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "uses as genuine", "reason to believe forged", "466: official certificate")
#ASSERT `offence under s 471` `the forged COE`
-- "in the same manner as if he had forged such document": s 466's punishment
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 471` `the forged COE`)'s section EQUALS "466"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 471` `the forged COE`)'s text EQUALS "You, B, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did dishonestly use as genuine a forged document, to wit, a Certificate of Entitlement purporting to be issued by the Land Transport Authority, by submitting it to Lim Motor Pte Ltd, which you had reason to believe to be a forged document, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 471 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 471` `the forged COE`)'s punishment EQUALS "in the same manner as if he had forged such document or electronic record: imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"

-- A plain forged letter used as genuine: s 465's punishment.
`a forged letter used` MEANS `forged document facts` (LIST "document", "fraudulently", "uses as genuine", "knows forged")
#ASSERT `offence under s 471` `a forged letter used`
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 471` `a forged letter used`)'s section EQUALS "465"
-- Neither knowledge nor reason to believe: no offence.
`an innocent user` MEANS `forged document facts` (LIST "document", "dishonestly", "uses as genuine")
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 471` `an innocent user`

-- s 474: possession, knowledge, intent, and a s 466 / s 467 description.
`a forged cheque held` MEANS `forged document facts` (LIST "document", "possession", "knows forged", "intending use as genuine", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT `offence under s 474` `a forged cheque held`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 474` `a forged cheque held`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 474` `the forged COE`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 474 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of having possession of a forged document or electronic record, knowing it to be forged, with intent to use it as genuine (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: has in his possession; knowing the same to be forged; intending that the same shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine."
-- No description in s 466 or s 467: no s 474 offence, however clear the rest.
`a forged letter held` MEANS `forged document facts` (LIST "document", "possession", "knows forged", "intending use as genuine")
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 474` `a forged letter held`
-- s 474 requires knowledge; reason to believe is not enough.
`a cheque held on suspicion` MEANS `forged document facts` (LIST "document", "possession", "reason to believe forged", "intending use as genuine", "467: valuable security")
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 474` `a cheque held on suspicion`

§§ `ss 472-473C, 475-477`

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Counterfeit Seal Facts`
`seal facts` keys MEANS
    `Counterfeit Seal Facts` WITH
        particulars      IS `test particulars for` "C"
        `the instrument` IS "a rubber stamp bearing the seal of the Registry of Marriages"
        `makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression` IS elem "makes" keys
        `has in his possession any such seal, plate or other instrument` IS elem "possession" keys
        `knowing the same to be counterfeit` IS elem "knowing counterfeit" keys
        `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under section 467` IS elem "for a s 467 forgery" keys
        `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under another section of this Chapter` IS elem "for another forgery" keys

#ASSERT `offence under s 472` (`seal facts` (LIST "makes", "for a s 467 forgery"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 473` (`seal facts` (LIST "makes", "for a s 467 forgery"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 473` (`seal facts` (LIST "possession", "knowing counterfeit", "for another forgery"))
-- possession without knowledge that it is counterfeit
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 473` (`seal facts` (LIST "possession", "for another forgery"))

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `False Instrument Equipment Facts`
`equipment facts` keys MEANS
    `False Instrument Equipment Facts` WITH
        particulars     IS `test particulars for` "D"
        `the equipment` IS "a card embosser and 40 blank magnetic-stripe cards"
        `makes it`      IS elem "makes" keys
        `has it in his custody or under his control` IS elem "custody" keys
        `to his knowledge it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument` IS elem "knows designed for false instruments" keys
        `it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument` IS elem "designed for instruments" keys
        `intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using it in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine` IS elem "intends a false instrument" keys
        `intends that by reason of so accepting it, that person does or does not do some act to his or any other person's prejudice` IS elem "intends prejudice" keys

#ASSERT `offence under s 473A` (`equipment facts` (LIST "custody", "knows designed for false instruments"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 473A` (`equipment facts` (LIST "custody", "designed for instruments"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 473B` (`equipment facts` (LIST "custody", "designed for instruments", "intends a false instrument", "intends prejudice"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 473B` (`equipment facts` (LIST "custody", "designed for instruments", "intends a false instrument"))

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Prejudice Facts`
`prejudice facts` keys MEANS
    `Prejudice Facts` WITH
        `result in his permanent or temporary loss of property` IS elem "(a)" keys
        `result in his being deprived of an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration` IS elem "(b)" keys
        `result in his being deprived of an opportunity to gain a financial advantage otherwise than by way of remuneration` IS elem "(c)" keys
        `result in somebody being given an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration from him` IS elem "(d)" keys
        `result in somebody being given an opportunity to gain a financial advantage from him otherwise than by way of remuneration` IS elem "(e)" keys
        `be the result of his having accepted a false instrument as genuine in connection with his performance of any duty` IS elem "(f)" keys
        `an act which the person has an enforceable duty to do` IS elem "(2) enforceable duty" keys
        `an omission to do an act which the person is not entitled to do` IS elem "(2) not entitled" keys
        `induced by a machine responding to the instrument` IS elem "(4) machine" keys

-- s 473C(1)(a), and (2) disregarding an act the person had an enforceable duty to do
#ASSERT `to a person's prejudice within section 473C` (`prejudice facts` (LIST "(a)"))
#ASSERT NOT `to a person's prejudice within section 473C` (`prejudice facts` (LIST "(a)", "(2) enforceable duty"))
-- s 473C(3)-(4): a machine's response is treated as prejudice
#ASSERT `to a person's prejudice within section 473C` (`prejudice facts` (LIST "(4) machine"))
#ASSERT NOT `to a person's prejudice within section 473C` (`prejudice facts` EMPTY)

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Counterfeit Mark Facts`
`mark facts` keys MEANS
    `Counterfeit Mark Facts` WITH
        particulars    IS `test particulars for` "E"
        `the material` IS "200 sheets of paper bearing a counterfeit watermark"
        `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document` IS elem "counterfeits" keys
        `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited` IS elem "possession" keys
        `intending that the device or mark shall be used to give the appearance of authenticity to a document then forged or thereafter to be forged on the material` IS elem "intending authenticity" keys
        `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document described in section 467` IS elem "467 document" keys
        `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document or electronic record other than those described in section 467` IS elem "other document" keys

#ASSERT `offence under s 475` (`mark facts` (LIST "counterfeits", "intending authenticity", "467 document"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 476` (`mark facts` (LIST "counterfeits", "intending authenticity", "467 document"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 476` (`mark facts` (LIST "possession", "intending authenticity", "other document"))
-- neither description answered: neither offence (an unknown is not "other than s 467")
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 476` (`mark facts` (LIST "possession", "intending authenticity"))

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Will or Security Destruction Facts`
`will facts` keys MEANS
    `Will or Security Destruction Facts` WITH
        particulars    IS `test particulars for` "F"
        `the document` IS "the last will of Tan Ah Kow dated 1 May 2015"
        `the act`      IS "destroy"
        fraudulently   IS elem "fraudulently" keys
        dishonestly    IS elem "dishonestly" keys
        `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` IS elem "intent to injure" keys
        `cancels, destroys or defaces` IS elem "destroys" keys
        `attempts to cancel, destroy or deface` IS elem "attempts to destroy" keys
        secretes       IS elem "secretes" keys
        `attempts to secrete` IS elem "attempts to secrete" keys
        `commits mischief in respect to such document` IS elem "mischief" keys
        `is or purports to be a will` IS elem "will" keys
        `is or purports to be an authority to adopt a child` IS elem "adoption" keys
        `is or purports to be a valuable security` IS elem "valuable security" keys

#ASSERT `offence under s 477` (`will facts` (LIST "dishonestly", "destroys", "will"))
#ASSERT (`charge under s 477` (`will facts` (LIST "dishonestly", "destroys", "will")))'s text EQUALS "You, F, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did dishonestly destroy a document which is or purports to be a will, to wit, the last will of Tan Ah Kow dated 1 May 2015, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 477 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- the attempt is the section's own limb
#ASSERT `offence under s 477` (`will facts` (LIST "intent to injure", "attempts to secrete", "valuable security"))
-- an ordinary letter is not within s 477
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 477` (`will facts` (LIST "dishonestly", "destroys"))

§§ `s 477A - falsification of accounts`

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Falsification of Accounts Facts`
`accounts facts` keys MEANS
    `Falsification of Accounts Facts` WITH
        particulars         IS `test particulars for` "Lim Mei Ling"
        `the capacity`      IS "a servant, to wit, an accounts executive of Tan Holdings Pte Ltd"
        `the falsification` IS "make a false entry in a payment voucher dated 3 March 2020, to wit, by recording a payment of $5,000 to Lim Trading, when no such payment was due, which voucher belonged to your employer"
        `being a clerk, officer or servant` IS elem "servant" keys
        `employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant` IS elem "acting as servant" keys
        `acts intentionally` IS elem "intentionally" keys
        `with intent to defraud` IS elem "intent to defraud" keys
        `destroys, alters, conceals, mutilates or falsifies` IS elem "falsifies" keys
        `makes or abets the making of any false entry in` IS elem "false entry" keys
        `omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in` IS elem "omits particular" keys
        `any book, electronic record, paper, writing, valuable security or account or a set thereof` IS elem "account" keys
        `belongs to or is in the possession of his employer` IS elem "employer's" keys
        `has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer` IS elem "received for employer" keys

`the false voucher` MEANS `accounts facts` (LIST "servant", "intentionally", "intent to defraud", "false entry", "account", "employer's")
#ASSERT `offence under s 477A` `the false voucher`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 477A` `the false voucher`)'s text EQUALS "You, Lim Mei Ling, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, being a servant, to wit, an accounts executive of Tan Holdings Pte Ltd, did intentionally and with intent to defraud make a false entry in a payment voucher dated 3 March 2020, to wit, by recording a payment of $5,000 to Lim Trading, when no such payment was due, which voucher belonged to your employer, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 477A of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 477A` `the false voucher`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
-- not a clerk, officer or servant (an outsider): no s 477A offence
`an outsider's false entry` MEANS `accounts facts` (LIST "intentionally", "intent to defraud", "false entry", "account", "employer's")
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 477A` `an outsider's false entry`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 477A` `an outsider's false entry`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 477A would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of falsification of accounts (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: being a clerk, officer or servant, or employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant."
-- no intent to defraud
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 477A` (`accounts facts` (LIST "servant", "intentionally", "false entry", "account", "employer's"))
-- a record that is not the employer's and was not received for him
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 477A` (`accounts facts` (LIST "servant", "intentionally", "intent to defraud", "falsifies", "account"))
-- received on the employer's behalf is enough
#ASSERT `offence under s 477A` (`accounts facts` (LIST "acting as servant", "intentionally", "intent to defraud", "omits particular", "account", "received for employer"))

§§ `ss 489A-489I - currency and bank notes`

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Currency Facts`
`currency facts` keys MEANS
    `Currency Facts` WITH
        particulars           IS `test particulars for` "G"
        `the currency`        IS "ten counterfeit Singapore $50 currency notes"
        `currency or a bank note` IS elem "currency" keys
        `a coin`              IS elem "coin" keys
        `the currency or bank note is forged or counterfeit` IS elem "counterfeit" keys
        `forges or counterfeits` IS elem "forges" keys
        `knowingly performs any part of the process of forging or counterfeiting` IS elem "part of process" keys
        `delivers or sells to, or buys or receives from, any other person` IS elem "delivers" keys
        `imports, exports or traffics in` IS elem "traffics" keys
        `uses as genuine`     IS elem "uses as genuine" keys
        `knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit` IS elem "knows counterfeit" keys
        `has in his possession` IS elem "possession" keys
        `intending to use the same as genuine or that it may be used as genuine` IS elem "intending use" keys
        `a die, machinery, instrument or material` IS elem "die" keys
        `makes, mends or performs any part of the process of making or mending` IS elem "makes die" keys
        `buys, sells or disposes of` IS elem "buys die" keys
        `for the purpose of being used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note` IS elem "die for counterfeiting" keys
        `knowing or having reason to believe that it is intended to be used for forging or counterfeiting any currency or bank note` IS elem "knows die for counterfeiting" keys
        `being within Singapore` IS elem "within Singapore" keys
        `abets the counterfeiting of any currency out of Singapore` IS elem "abets abroad" keys
        fraudulently          IS elem "fraudulently" keys
        dishonestly           IS elem "dishonestly" keys
        `performs on any coin an operation which diminishes the weight or alters the composition of that coin` IS elem "alters coin" keys
        `performs on any currency an operation which alters the appearance of that currency` IS elem "alters appearance" keys
        `with the intention that that currency will pass as currency of a different description` IS elem "to pass as other currency" keys
        `delivers to any other person as genuine, or as currency of a different description` IS elem "delivers altered" keys
        `attempts to induce any person to receive it as genuine, or as currency of a different description` IS elem "attempts to pass altered" keys
        `knows or has reason to believe that an operation mentioned in section 489F or 489G has been performed on it` IS elem "knows altered" keys
        `knows or has reason to believe that an offence defined in section 489F or 489G has been committed with respect to it` IS elem "knows offence on it" keys

`passing a fake $50` MEANS `currency facts` (LIST "currency", "counterfeit", "uses as genuine", "knows counterfeit")
#ASSERT `offence under s 489B` `passing a fake $50`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 489B` `passing a fake $50`)'s text EQUALS "You, G, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did use as genuine forged or counterfeit currency or bank notes, to wit, ten counterfeit Singapore $50 currency notes, knowing or having reason to believe the same to be forged or counterfeit, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 489B of the Penal Code 1871."
-- passing a note one has no reason to suspect: no offence
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 489B` (`currency facts` (LIST "currency", "counterfeit", "uses as genuine"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 489C` (`currency facts` (LIST "currency", "counterfeit", "possession", "knows counterfeit", "intending use"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 489C` (`currency facts` (LIST "currency", "counterfeit", "possession", "knows counterfeit"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 489A` (`currency facts` (LIST "currency", "part of process"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 489D` (`currency facts` (LIST "die", "possession", "knows die for counterfeiting"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 489E` (`currency facts` (LIST "within Singapore", "abets abroad"))
-- s 489F Explanation: scooping out part of a coin and filling the cavity alters its composition
#ASSERT `offence under s 489F` (`currency facts` (LIST "coin", "fraudulently", "alters coin"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 489F` (`currency facts` (LIST "coin", "alters coin"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 489G` (`currency facts` (LIST "currency", "alters appearance", "to pass as other currency"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 489H` (`currency facts` (LIST "currency", "attempts to pass altered", "knows altered"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 489I` (`currency facts` (LIST "currency", "possession", "knows offence on it", "intending use"))
#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 489A`'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS JUST 240

-- s 489A(2)
GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Currency Description Facts`
`description facts` keys MEANS
    `Currency Description Facts` WITH
        `a promissory note or engagement for the payment of money to bearer on demand` IS elem "bearer note" keys
        `issued by any person carrying on the business of banking in any part of the world` IS elem "banker" keys
        `issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory` IS elem "government" keys
        `intended to be used as equivalent to, or as a substitute for, money` IS elem "as money" keys
        `metal used as money` IS elem "metal" keys
        `stamped and issued by or under the authority of the government of any country or territory in order to be so used` IS elem "stamped by government" keys
        `a currency note` IS elem "currency note" keys
        `legal tender in the country or territory in which it is issued` IS elem "legal tender" keys

#ASSERT `bank note within section 489A(2)` (`description facts` (LIST "bearer note", "banker"))
#ASSERT `bank note within section 489A(2)` (`description facts` (LIST "bearer note", "government", "as money"))
#ASSERT NOT `bank note within section 489A(2)` (`description facts` (LIST "bearer note", "government"))
#ASSERT `currency within section 489A(2)` (`description facts` (LIST "metal", "stamped by government", "legal tender"))
#ASSERT NOT `currency within section 489A(2)` (`description facts` (LIST "currency note"))

§ `Chapter 21 - defamation`

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Defamation Facts`
`defamation facts` keys MEANS
    `Defamation Facts` WITH
        particulars           IS `test particulars for` "A"
        victim                IS "Z"
        `victim described as` IS ""
        `victim pronoun`      IS he
        `the imputation`      IS "the said Z had stolen the watch of one B"
        `the means`           IS "saying the words 'Z is an honest man; he never stole B's watch'"
        `by words either spoken or intended to be read` IS elem "words" keys
        `by signs`            IS elem "signs" keys
        `by visible representations` IS elem "picture" keys
        `makes or publishes any imputation concerning any person` IS elem "imputation" keys
        `intending to harm the reputation of such person` IS elem "intending harm" keys
        `knowing or having reason to believe that such imputation will harm the reputation of such person` IS elem "knowing harm" keys
        `the harm is harm to reputation within Explanation 4` IS elem "Expl 4 harm" keys
        `imputes anything to a deceased person` IS elem "deceased" keys
        `would harm the reputation of that person if living` IS elem "harm if living" keys
        `is intended to be hurtful to the feelings of his family or other near relatives` IS elem "hurtful to family" keys
        `the want of good faith appears` IS elem "want of good faith" keys
        `the imputation is true` IS elem "true" keys
        `it is for the public good that the imputation should be made or published` IS elem "public good" keys
        `expresses an opinion respecting the conduct of any person touching the discharge of his public functions, or his character so far as it appears in that conduct` IS elem "2nd" keys
        `expresses an opinion respecting the conduct of any person touching any public question, and his character so far as it appears in that conduct` IS elem "3rd" keys
        `publishes a substantially true report of the proceedings of a court of justice or of Parliament, or of their result` IS elem "4th" keys
        `expresses an opinion respecting the merits of a decided case, or the conduct of a party, witness or agent in it, or his character so far as it appears in that conduct` IS elem "5th" keys
        `expresses an opinion respecting the merits of a performance its author has submitted to the judgment of the public, or the author's character so far as it appears in it` IS elem "6th" keys
        `passes censure on the conduct of another over whom the accused has lawful authority, in matters to which that authority relates` IS elem "7th" keys
        `prefers an accusation against the person to one having lawful authority over him with respect to the subject matter of the accusation` IS elem "8th" keys
        `makes an imputation on the character of another for the protection of the interests of the person making it or of any other person, or for the public good` IS elem "9th" keys
        `conveys a caution to one person against another, intended for the good of that person or of one in whom he is interested, or for the public good` IS elem "10th" keys

-- s 499 illus (a): "Z is an honest man; he never stole B's watch", meant to
-- make it believed Z did - ironical (Explanation 3). "This is defamation,
-- unless it falls within one of the exceptions."
`illus 499(a)` MEANS `defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "intending harm", "Expl 4 harm")
#ASSERT defames `illus 499(a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 500` `illus 499(a)`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 500` `illus 499(a)`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did defame one Z by saying the words 'Z is an honest man; he never stole B's watch', imputing that the said Z had stolen the watch of one B, intending to harm the reputation of the said Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 500 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 499 illus (b): asked who stole B's watch, A points to Z - a sign.
#ASSERT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "signs", "imputation", "intending harm", "Expl 4 harm"))
-- s 499 illus (c): A draws a picture of Z running away with B's watch.
#ASSERT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "picture", "imputation", "intending harm", "Expl 4 harm"))
-- Explanation 4: an imputation that lowers no one's estimate of Z harms no reputation.
#ASSERT NOT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "intending harm"))
-- Explanation 1: a deceased person.
#ASSERT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "deceased", "harm if living", "hurtful to family"))
#ASSERT NOT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "deceased", "harm if living"))

-- First Exception: true AND for the public good; true alone is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "intending harm", "Expl 4 harm", "true", "public good"))
#ASSERT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "intending harm", "Expl 4 harm", "true"))
-- Third Exception illus: an opinion in good faith on Z's conduct in petitioning Government on a public question.
#ASSERT NOT defames (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "3rd"))
-- Fifth Exception illus (a): "Z's evidence ... so contradictory that he must be stupid or dishonest" - within, in good faith.
`illus 499 Exc 5(a)` MEANS `defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "5th")
#ASSERT `the imputation falls within an Exception to s 499` `illus 499 Exc 5(a)`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 500` `illus 499 Exc 5(a)`
-- Fifth Exception illus (b): "a man without veracity" - an opinion NOT founded on Z's conduct as a witness: not within.
#ASSERT `offence under s 500` (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm"))
-- Sixth Exception illus (d): "Z's book is foolish, Z must be a weak man" - within.
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 500` (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "6th"))
-- Seventh Exception illus: a banker censuring his cashier in good faith.
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 500` (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "7th"))
-- Eighth Exception illus: A in good faith accuses Z before a Magistrate.
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 500` (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "8th"))
-- Ninth Exception illus (a): a shopkeeper to his manager, "Sell nothing to Z unless he pays ready money".
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 500` (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "9th"))
-- Explanation to Exceptions: good faith is presumed - but where the want of it appears, the Ninth Exception fails.
`the shopkeeper in bad faith` MEANS `defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "9th", "want of good faith")
#ASSERT `offence under s 500` `the shopkeeper in bad faith`
-- ... and good faith is not part of the First or Fourth Exception.
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 500` (`defamation facts` (LIST "words", "imputation", "knowing harm", "Expl 4 harm", "4th", "want of good faith"))
-- The refusal when an Exception applies.
#ASSERT (`charge under s 500` `illus 499 Exc 5(a)`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 500 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of defamation (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: not within any of the cases excepted (the First to Tenth Exceptions); the elements of section 499 taken together."

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Defamatory Matter Facts`
`matter facts` keys MEANS
    `Defamatory Matter Facts` WITH
        particulars          IS `test particulars for` "H"
        `the matter`         IS "500 copies of a pamphlet"
        `the person defamed` IS "one Z"
        `prints or engraves any matter` IS elem "prints" keys
        `knowing or having good reason to believe that such matter is defamatory of any person` IS elem "knows defamatory" keys
        `sells or offers for sale any printed or engraved substance` IS elem "sells" keys
        `the substance contains defamatory matter` IS elem "defamatory" keys
        `knowing that it contains such matter` IS elem "knows contents" keys

#ASSERT `offence under s 501` (`matter facts` (LIST "prints", "knows defamatory"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 501` (`matter facts` (LIST "prints"))
#ASSERT `offence under s 502` (`matter facts` (LIST "sells", "defamatory", "knows contents"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 502` (`matter facts` (LIST "sells", "knows contents"))

§ `Chapter 22 - criminal intimidation, insult and annoyance`

§§ `Chan Yok Tuang v Public Prosecutor [2008] SGHC 137 - the reference row's fixtures`

GIVEN words IS A STRING
      keys  IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Criminal Intimidation Facts`
`Chan Yok Tuang's threat` words keys MEANS
    `Criminal Intimidation Facts` WITH
        particulars           IS Particulars WITH
                                   accused            IS "Chan Yok Tuang"
                                   date               IS "16 May 2007"
                                   time               IS ""
                                   place              IS "the Central Police Division lockup"
                                   `co-accused`       IS ""
                                   `common intention` IS FALSE
        victim                IS "SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee"
        `victim described as` IS ""
        `victim pronoun`      IS she
        `threat words`        IS words
        language              IS "Hokkien"
        `threatened the victim` IS elem "threatened" keys
        person                IS elem "person" keys
        reputation            IS elem "reputation" keys
        property              IS elem "property" keys
        `person of one in whom interested` IS elem "person of one interested" keys
        `reputation of one in whom interested` IS elem "reputation of one interested" keys
        `cause alarm`         IS elem "alarm" keys
        `do an act not legally bound to do` IS elem "do an act" keys
        `omit an act legally entitled to do` IS elem "omit an act" keys
        death                 IS elem "death" keys
        `grievous hurt`       IS elem "grievous hurt" keys
        `the destruction of any property by fire` IS elem "fire" keys
        `an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for 7 years or more` IS elem "serious offence" keys
        `by an anonymous communication` IS elem "anonymous" keys
        `by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes` IS elem "concealed" keys

-- FIXTURE A: the facts as they were - injury to the person, no intent to alarm. Refused.
`CYT as they were` MEANS `Chan Yok Tuang's threat` "I will shoot her to death" (LIST "threatened", "person", "death")
#ASSERT NOT `commits criminal intimidation` `CYT as they were`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 506` `CYT as they were`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 506 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal intimidation (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do; the elements of section 503 taken together."

-- FIXTURE B: the one leaf the revision turned on, flipped.
`CYT with intent to alarm` MEANS `Chan Yok Tuang's threat` "I will shoot her to death" (LIST "threatened", "person", "alarm", "death")
#ASSERT `offence under s 506` `CYT with intent to alarm`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 506` `CYT with intent to alarm`)'s text EQUALS "You, Chan Yok Tuang, are charged that you, on or about 16 May 2007, at the Central Police Division lockup, Singapore, did commit criminal intimidation by threatening to cause injury to the person of SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee; to wit, by uttering \"I will shoot her to death\" in Hokkien at her, with intent to cause alarm to the said SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 506 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 506` `CYT with intent to alarm`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
-- FIXTURE C: aggravation withdrawn - same offence, the first limb's punishment.
`CYT not aggravated` MEANS `Chan Yok Tuang's threat` "I will slap her" (LIST "threatened", "person", "alarm")
#ASSERT `offence under s 506` `CYT not aggravated`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 506` `CYT not aggravated`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
-- The Explanation to s 503: a threat to the reputation of a deceased person one is interested in.
#ASSERT `commits criminal intimidation` (`Chan Yok Tuang's threat` "" (LIST "threatened", "reputation of one interested", "do an act"))

-- s 503 illus: A, to make B desist from a civil suit, threatens to burn B's
-- house. "A is guilty of criminal intimidation." Property; the omission limb;
-- and, being a threat by fire, the second limb of s 506.
`illus 503` MEANS `Criminal Intimidation Facts` WITH
    particulars           IS `test particulars for` "A"
    victim                IS "B"
    `victim described as` IS "the plaintiff in the said civil suit"
    `victim pronoun`      IS he
    `threat words`        IS ""
    language              IS ""
    `threatened the victim` IS TRUE
    person                IS FALSE
    reputation            IS FALSE
    property              IS TRUE
    `person of one in whom interested`     IS FALSE
    `reputation of one in whom interested` IS FALSE
    `cause alarm`         IS FALSE
    `do an act not legally bound to do`    IS FALSE
    `omit an act legally entitled to do`   IS TRUE
    death                 IS FALSE
    `grievous hurt`       IS FALSE
    `the destruction of any property by fire` IS TRUE
    `an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for 7 years or more` IS FALSE
    `by an anonymous communication` IS FALSE
    `by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `commits criminal intimidation` `illus 503`
#ASSERT `the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` `illus 503`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 506` `illus 503`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did commit criminal intimidation by threatening to cause injury to the property of B, the plaintiff in the said civil suit, with intent to cause the said B to omit to do an act which he is legally entitled to do, as the means of avoiding the execution of the said threat, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 506 of the Penal Code 1871."

§§ `s 506 - the "7 years or more" threshold, on the helper (notes/PLAN.md §3.5)`

-- exactly 7 years (s 489F: 84 months) counts, by s 41; 5 years (s 469) does not
#ASSERT `punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more` `punishment prescribed by s 489F`
#ASSERT NOT `punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more` `punishment prescribed by s 469`
#ASSERT `punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more` `punishment prescribed by s 467`
#ASSERT NOT `punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more` `punishment prescribed by s 506`
-- a threat to commit forgery for the purpose of cheating (s 468, 10 years) falls in the second limb
`a threat to forge` MEANS `Chan Yok Tuang's threat` "" (append (LIST "threatened", "reputation", "do an act") (`included if` (`punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more` `punishment prescribed by s 468`) "serious offence"))
#ASSERT `the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` `a threat to forge`

§§ `s 507 - anonymous communication`

`an anonymous letter` MEANS `Chan Yok Tuang's threat` "" (LIST "threatened", "person", "alarm", "anonymous")
#ASSERT `offence under s 507` `an anonymous letter`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 507` `CYT with intent to alarm`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 507` `an anonymous letter`)'s text EQUALS "You, Chan Yok Tuang, are charged that you, on or about 16 May 2007, at the Central Police Division lockup, Singapore, did commit criminal intimidation by threatening to cause injury to the person of SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee, with intent to cause alarm to the said SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee, by an anonymous communication, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 507 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 507` `CYT with intent to alarm`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 507 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal intimidation by an anonymous communication (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: by an anonymous communication, or by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat comes."
#ASSERT `punishment prescribed by s 507`'s imprisonment EQUALS `shall be punished with`

§§ `s 504 - intentional insult`

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH AN `Intentional Insult Facts`
`insult facts` keys MEANS
    `Intentional Insult Facts` WITH
        particulars           IS `test particulars for` "J"
        victim                IS "K"
        `victim described as` IS ""
        `victim pronoun`      IS he
        `the insult`          IS "uttering the words 'you are a thief' at him"
        `intentionally insults` IS elem "insults" keys
        `thereby gives provocation to any person` IS elem "provokes" keys
        `intending that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence` IS elem "intending breach" keys
        `knowing it to be likely that such provocation will cause him to break the public peace or to commit any other offence` IS elem "knowing breach likely" keys

#ASSERT `offence under s 504` (`insult facts` (LIST "insults", "provokes", "knowing breach likely"))
#ASSERT (`charge under s 504` (`insult facts` (LIST "insults", "provokes", "knowing breach likely")))'s text EQUALS "You, J, are charged that you, on or about 1 March 2026, at Blk 1 Jurong West Street 1, Singapore, did intentionally insult one K by uttering the words 'you are a thief' at him, and thereby gave provocation to the said K, knowing it to be likely that such provocation would cause him to break the public peace, or to commit any other offence, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 504 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- an insult that provokes, without the intention or knowledge
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 504` (`insult facts` (LIST "insults", "provokes"))

§§ `s 505 - statements conducing to public mischief, and its Exception`

GIVEN keys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Public Mischief Statement Facts`
`statement facts` keys MEANS
    `Public Mischief Statement Facts` WITH
        particulars      IS `test particulars for` "L"
        `the statement`  IS "a post stating that the water supply had been poisoned"
        `makes, publishes or circulates any statement, rumour or report` IS elem "publishes" keys
        `with intent to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty` IS elem "(a) intent" keys
        `likely to cause a serviceman to mutiny or otherwise disregard or fail in his duty` IS elem "(a) likely" keys
        `with intent to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity` IS elem "(b) intent" keys
        `likely to cause fear or alarm to the public whereby any person may be induced to commit an offence against the State or the public tranquillity` IS elem "(b) likely" keys
        `with intent to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community` IS elem "(c) intent" keys
        `likely to incite any class or community of persons to commit any offence against any other class or community` IS elem "(c) likely" keys
        `has reasonable grounds for believing that the statement, rumour or report is true` IS elem "reasonable grounds" keys

#ASSERT `offence under s 505` (`statement facts` (LIST "publishes", "(b) likely"))
-- the Exception: reasonable grounds for believing it true, and no such intent
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 505` (`statement facts` (LIST "publishes", "(b) likely", "reasonable grounds"))
-- ... but not where the intent is there (FORK DD-11)
#ASSERT `offence under s 505` (`statement facts` (LIST "publishes", "(b) intent", "(b) likely", "reasonable grounds"))
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 505` (`statement facts` (LIST "publishes"))
